{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q3068413","formula":"C₂₄H₂₀Cl₂N₂OS","hill":"C24H20Cl2N2OS","elements":["H","C","N","O","S","Cl"],"composition":{"C":24.0,"H":20.0,"N":2.0,"O":1.0,"S":1.0,"Cl":2.0},"names":{"en":"Fenticonazole","uk":"Фентиконазол"},"descriptions":{"en":"Fenticonazole is an imidazole antifungal drug, used locally as the nitrate in the treatment of vulvovaginal candidiasis. It is active against a range of organisms including Trichophyton mentagrophytes, Malassezia furfur, and Candida albicans. Fenticonazole has also been shown to exhibit antibacterial action, with a spectrum of activity that includes bacteria commonly associated with superinfected fungal skin and vaginal infections, and antiparasitic action against the protozoan Trichomonas vaginalis.","uk":"Фентиконазол — синтетичний протигрибковий препарат, що належить до підгрупи імідазолів класу азолів для місцевого застосування."},"fame":10,"pubchemCid":51755,"mass":455.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC=C(C=C1)SC2=CC=C(C=C2)COC(CN3C=CN=C3)C4=C(C=C(C=C4)Cl)Cl","inchikey":"ZCJYUTQZBAIHBS-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-[2-(2,4-dichlorophenyl)-2-[(4-phenylsulfanylphenyl)methoxy]ethyl]imidazole","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"51755","atoms":50,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-4.487,"y":0.085,"z":-2.438,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-6.385,"y":3.553,"z":1.215,"el":"Cl"},{"x":4.642,"y":2.648,"z":-0.361,"el":"S"},{"x":-1.286,"y":-0.403,"z":-0.088,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.889,"y":-3.229,"z":0.374,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.197,"y":-5.09,"z":-0.589,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.612,"y":-0.9,"z":-0.198,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.765,"y":-2.117,"z":0.724,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.574,"y":0.221,"z":0.127,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.057,"y":0.677,"z":-0.986,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.446,"y":0.714,"z":-0.831,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.553,"y":0.736,"z":1.414,"el":"C"},{"x":0.345,"y":1.161,"z":